      "id": 85946720,
      "body": "How do you balance the test batching with testing individual PRs enough to feel confident they will be approved?\nMy immediate thought was having good guidelines around unit tests vs integration tests. I can also see it helping to push for smaller PRs since it’s easier to have high confidence in smaller changes. It seems like you need your SDLC set up to support batch testing though since I wouldn’t want to batch 3 PRs that have 1000+ lines changed.\nThe batch testing could also cause problems since it might not be clear which of the changes is causing the issue. How do you deal with that?",
      "body_json": {
        "type": "doc",
        "attrs": {
          "schemaVersion": "v1"
        },
        "content": [
